# RaffoSynth for WebCLAP

RaffoSynth (a Minimoog emulator: Nicolas Roulet's RaffoSynth with AnClark's DPF plugin layer (RaffoSynth-XT)), ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official release.

- RaffoSynth: https://github.com/AnClark/RaffoSynth-XT (commit c9b28fd, GPL-3.0-or-later)
- [DPF](https://github.com/DISTRHO/DPF) (commit 4238e1c), the DISTRHO Plugin Framework the plugin is written with
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-raffosynth.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

## License

The bundle as a whole is licensed under the **GNU General Public License, version 3 or later** (`LICENSE`).

RaffoSynth-XT is GPL-3.0-or-later (`licenses/RaffoSynth-XT-GPL-3.0.txt`). The synthesizer it builds on, RaffoSynth by Nicolas Roulet, is MIT-licensed (`licenses/RaffoSynth-MIT.txt`); DPF is ISC (`licenses/DPF-ISC.txt`). Both are compatible with the GPL; `module.wasm` as a whole is distributed under the GPL-3.0-or-later.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

The bundle holds the DSP only (`module.wasm`): DPF's own CLAP wrapper compiled to WebAssembly. The plugin's graphical
editor is not part of it, hosts show the plugin's parameters instead.

